msgid ""
"We are ready to build the Redox operating system image. Skip ahead to "
"[Configuration Settings](./configuration-settings.md) if you want to build "
"for a different CPU architecture or with different filesystem contents."
msgstr ""

#: src/building-redox.md:99
msgid "Build all system components and programs"
msgstr ""

#: src/building-redox.md:101
msgid ""
"To build all the components and packages to be included in the filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: src/building-redox.md:111
msgid ""
"This will build the target `build/x86_64/desktop/harddrive.img`, which can "
"be run in a virtual machine."
msgstr ""

#: src/building-redox.md:113
msgid ""
"Give it a while. Redox is big. Read the [`make all` (first run)](./build-"
"phases.md#make-all-first-run) section for an explanation of what the `make "
"all` command does."
msgstr ""

#: src/building-redox.md:115
msgid ""
"💡 **Tip:** the filesystem parts are merged into the final system image "
"using the [FUSE](https://github.com/libfuse/libfuse) library. The "
"`bootstrap.sh` script installs `libfuse` automatically. If you encounter "
"problems with the final Redox image, verify `libfuse` is installed and that "
"you are able to use it."
msgstr ""
